IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ca14-accused`

-- Crimes Regulations 2019 -- the screening bodies and laws prescribed for Part VIIC Division 6 of the Crimes Act 1914 (work
-- with children, people with disability and funded aged care), read from the deposited Regulations so the spent-conviction
-- question can check whether the body asking is prescribed instead of assuming it. A module beside ca14-accused.l4; it calls
-- that module's `Must I disclose this conviction`, `Who is asking about my conviction` and `Answer`, restating none of them.
--
-- SEAT: the person with a conviction, as in ca14-accused.l4. "My Commonwealth conviction is spent. I am applying for a
-- working-with-children check, or NDIS or aged-care worker screening. May the screening body be told about it and take it
-- into account?"
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 5, compilation date 13 December 2025, includes amendments F2025L01544 (register id F2025C01226),
-- deposited at ../../../crimes-regulations-2019/registers/source-bundle/F2019L01005.txt (retrieved 2026-10-23).
--
-- IN: regs 20 (children: ss 85ZZGB-85ZZGD), 20A (people with disability: ss 85ZZGI-85ZZGK). No person, body or law is
-- prescribed for funded aged care (ss 85ZZGP-85ZZGR): the Regulations have no such regulation (NOTES.md finding 17).
-- OUT: reg 21 and Schedule 2 (the s 85ZZH(k) persons, purposes and offences, for bodies other than screening bodies), and
-- the rest of the Regulations (forms, controlled operations, forensic procedures), which do not address this seat's question.

§ `Crimes Regulations 2019 -- may a screening body be told about my spent conviction`

§§ `regs 20, 20A -- the prescribed screening bodies`

DECLARE `The screening body` IS ONE OF
    -- reg 20 items 1-10 (children)
    `NSW: the Children's Guardian (working with children check)`
    `Vic: the Secretary under the Worker Screening Act 2020`
    `Qld: the chief executive under the Working with Children (Risk Management and Screening) Act 2000 (blue card)`
    `Qld: the Queensland College of Teachers`
    `WA: the CEO under the Working with Children (Criminal Record Checking) Act 2004`
    `SA: the central assessment unit under the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016`
    `Tas: the Registrar under the Registration to Work with Vulnerable People Act 2013`
    `ACT: the Commissioner under the Working with Vulnerable People (Background Checking) Act 2011`
    `ACT: an independent advisor under the Working with Vulnerable People (Background Checking) Act 2011`
    `NT: the Screening Authority under the Care and Protection of Children Act 2007`
    -- reg 20A items 1-5 (people with disability) not already named above
    `NSW: the Screening Agency under the National Disability Insurance Scheme (Worker Checks) Act 2018`
    `Qld: the chief executive under the Disability Services Act 2006`
    `WA: the CEO under the National Disability Insurance Scheme (Worker Screening) Act 2020`
    `NT: the Screening Agency under the National Disability Insurance Scheme (Worker Clearance) Act 2020`
    `another person or body, such as an aged care worker screening body`

DECLARE `The work` IS ONE OF
    `work with children`
    `work with people with disability (NDIS worker screening)`
    `work with people accessing funded aged care`

-- reg 20: "For the purposes of sections 85ZZGB, 85ZZGC and 85ZZGD of the Act, the persons and bodies mentioned in column 1 of
-- an item in the following table, and the laws mentioned in column 2 ..., are prescribed to the extent that those laws relate
-- to persons working, or seeking to work, with children". reg 20A: the same for ss 85ZZGI-85ZZGK, to the extent the laws "are
-- NDIS worker screening laws" and relate to work with people with disability. The Victorian Secretary, the SA central
-- assessment unit (under the Disability Inclusion Act 2018 (SA) for disability), the Tasmanian Registrar and the ACT
-- Commissioner appear in both tables.
GIVEN `the body` IS A `The screening body`
      `the work` IS A `The work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is prescribed for the work` IF
    CONSIDER `the work`
    WHEN `work with children` THEN
             `the body` EQUALS `NSW: the Children's Guardian (working with children check)`
          OR `the body` EQUALS `Vic: the Secretary under the Worker Screening Act 2020`
          OR `the body` EQUALS `Qld: the chief executive under the Working with Children (Risk Management and Screening) Act 2000 (blue card)`
          OR `the body` EQUALS `Qld: the Queensland College of Teachers`
          OR `the body` EQUALS `WA: the CEO under the Working with Children (Criminal Record Checking) Act 2004`
          OR `the body` EQUALS `SA: the central assessment unit under the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016`
          OR `the body` EQUALS `Tas: the Registrar under the Registration to Work with Vulnerable People Act 2013`
          OR `the body` EQUALS `ACT: the Commissioner under the Working with Vulnerable People (Background Checking) Act 2011`
          OR `the body` EQUALS `ACT: an independent advisor under the Working with Vulnerable People (Background Checking) Act 2011`
          OR `the body` EQUALS `NT: the Screening Authority under the Care and Protection of Children Act 2007`
    WHEN `work with people with disability (NDIS worker screening)` THEN
             `the body` EQUALS `NSW: the Screening Agency under the National Disability Insurance Scheme (Worker Checks) Act 2018`
          OR `the body` EQUALS `Vic: the Secretary under the Worker Screening Act 2020`
          OR `the body` EQUALS `Qld: the chief executive under the Disability Services Act 2006`
          OR `the body` EQUALS `WA: the CEO under the National Disability Insurance Scheme (Worker Screening) Act 2020`
          OR `the body` EQUALS `SA: the central assessment unit under the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016`
          OR `the body` EQUALS `Tas: the Registrar under the Registration to Work with Vulnerable People Act 2013`
          OR `the body` EQUALS `ACT: the Commissioner under the Working with Vulnerable People (Background Checking) Act 2011`
          OR `the body` EQUALS `NT: the Screening Agency under the National Disability Insurance Scheme (Worker Clearance) Act 2020`
    -- no regulation prescribes anyone for ss 85ZZGP-85ZZGR
    WHEN `work with people accessing funded aged care` THEN FALSE

@export Is this screening body prescribed by the Crimes Regulations to be told about, and take into account, spent convictions for this kind of work (regs 20, 20A)?
GIVEN `the body` IS A `The screening body` @desc Which screening body is checking you, by State or Territory
      `the work` IS A `The work` @desc The kind of work the check is for: with children, with people with disability (NDIS worker screening), or with people accessing funded aged care
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the screening body prescribed` IF `the body is prescribed for the work` `the body` `the work`

@export My conviction may be spent. Must I disclose it to this screening body, and may the body take it into account (ss 85ZV, 85ZW, Division 6, regs 20, 20A)?
GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are being asked
      `it is a State offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conviction is for an offence against a State law (including the ACT and NT, which Part VIIC counts as States), rather than a Commonwealth or external Territory offence
      `the body` IS A `The screening body` @desc Which screening body is checking you, by State or Territory
      `the work` IS A `The work` @desc The kind of work the check is for
      `I was pardoned for a reason other than wrongful conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been granted a pardon for the offence for a reason other than that you were wrongly convicted
      `I was sentenced to imprisonment for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were sentenced to imprisonment for the offence
      `the months of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc The length of that sentence of imprisonment, in months (0 if none)
      `the day of the conviction` IS A DATE @desc The day you were convicted (or found guilty and discharged without conviction)
      `I was dealt with as a minor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were dealt with as a minor (a juvenile) for the conviction
      `a later offence in the waiting period stops it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were later convicted of another offence committed during the waiting period, on indictment or by a State or foreign court, or the summary court ordered that the earlier conviction not become spent
      `the day of the later conviction` IS A DATE @desc The day of that later conviction (ignored if there is none)
      `I was dealt with as a minor for the later offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were dealt with as a minor for the later conviction
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Must I disclose my conviction`
`Must I disclose this conviction to the screening body` MEANS
    `Must I disclose this conviction` `the day asked about` `it is a State offence` `who is asking` `I was pardoned for a reason other than wrongful conviction` `I was sentenced to imprisonment for it` `the months of imprisonment` `the day of the conviction` `I was dealt with as a minor` `a later offence in the waiting period stops it` `the day of the later conviction` `I was dealt with as a minor for the later offence`
    WHERE
        -- A prescribed body is within Division 6; a body the Regulations do not prescribe is, for Part VIIC, an ordinary
        -- person asking for an ordinary purpose.
        `who is asking` MEANS
            IF `the body is prescribed for the work` `the body` `the work`
            THEN `a screening body for work with children, people with disability or aged care`
            ELSE `an employer, landlord, insurer or anyone else for an ordinary purpose`
